WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.760
- I have a bit of a
history with monorails.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.694
Back in 2016, I visited the Wuppertal
suspended monorail in Germany,

00:00:06.694 --> 00:00:10.770
and I said that monorails are
almost always a bad idea.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:13.170
Monorail enthusiasts
sent me angry messages,

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.490
but I stand by that.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:18.870
In 2020, I visited one of the last surviving
Roadmachines cargo monorails.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.860
They were actually useful and practical,
but they were temporary constructions

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.860
designed for having cargo
hauled around work sites.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:29.280
And they've been replaced by modern
heavy construction equipment.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.160
Monorails are usually bad ideas,

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.106
because the track has to be either
elevated or in a trench,

00:00:35.106 --> 00:00:38.910
and because switches at junctions
involve moving the whole track.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.720
In almost every case, a monorail is
a worse and more expensive idea

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.273
than light rail, or a tram, or a bus.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.420
But. While I was researching
a while ago,

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.300
I found a type of monorail
that is useful and practical

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.490
and better than any
alternative for its job.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.910
And not only is it still in use,
new versions of it are being built.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.740
So I reached out to the
company that makes them

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:02.070
and I asked them, "Can I
have a go on one, please?"

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.173
This is the Monorack.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.530
- We build mainly ropeways.
That's our main business.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:18.870
Everything with the rope.
Aerial tramways, chair lifts, ski lifts.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:23.040
And Monorack is a Garaventa product
since nearly 45 years.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.695
In 1978 I think, or '79.

00:01:25.695 --> 00:01:29.760
Some two years after the petrol Monorack,
they start with electrical Monoracks.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.730
They installed mainly in the Alp area.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.090
Germany, Switzerland, a
lot of Monoracks in Italy,

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:39.210
but also Canada, Sweden, Asia.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.560
All over the world we have more
or less about 800 Monoracks.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.850
The petrol Monoracks are mainly
installed in the agriculture area.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.040
The electrical Monorack usually is quiet,

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.170
but here the customer made his own box.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.960
That's the reason why it's
still a little bit loud!

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.060
- The invention that
makes this thing so useful

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.290
is down on the track.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:01.650
This is a rack railway,
so the track has grooves

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.260
and the cogs onboard
the train lock into it.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.870
That means it can climb
very steep hills like this

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.330
and take tight corners
with no risk of slipping.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:12.420
Having just one lightweight rail
means it doesn't take up much room.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.120
It can go around tight corners
and it's easy to install.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.520
Being elevated, means it
can go over rough terrain

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.250
and if there's rain or mud below,
it doesn't matter.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.770
I genuinely can't think
of a better solution

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:25.590
for regularly, safely,
moving things up and down

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.690
steep, rough terrain like this.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:32.760
- Every Monorack is based on a brake,
and on a engine chassis.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.122
And what's between the two chassis
is up to the customer,

00:02:37.122 --> 00:02:41.130
we can choose different models,
different chairs,

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.770
whatever the customer needs or wants.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.630
You can see the charging rails.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:47.790
If the customer wants two or three,

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.950
he can choose two or
three charging points.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:53.250
Normally we have only one,
in one of the end stations.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.580
- I know this sounds like an advert,
I promise it isn't.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:00.870
I just got actually properly enthusiastic
at being proved wrong.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:03.213
There are useful monorails in the world.

00:03:03.213 --> 00:03:05.616
And this? This is one of them.

